In my experience, monsters avoid a shrine not a room with
an altar.  If there is a priest in the room, it is a shrine.
If they are avoiding the room I think you have a co-aligned
priest with you.  Killing the priest is one option, likely
not the one you want to try.  Monsters would stop avoiding
the room but the price may be too high.  If it's just a
room with an altar, you are being impatient.  Get some
puddings to follow you; they are very slow.

> My goal, to sac until I get Mojo.

Then never pray until you have it.  The chance per #offer
starts out at 1-in-10 and that only applies when you don't
get hopefull or inadequate messages.  In general if you've
been seeing four-leafed clovers that's when the 1-in-10
chances start and not until.

> Being an impatient sort I want to know if it would be possible to bypass
> sacrificing beasts. Ilsa would just stand on Tyr's altar, #pray and hope
> that Tyr gives the magical hammer?

Not possible and it will completely take away any possibility
that you will receive your gift artifact.  Offer and prayer
are opposites this way.  Since you're lawfull, there is one
artifact you can get from prayer and most people don't want
it to happen until a time of their choice.  It's Excalibur
when your crowned.



